    "hairscripts_hair_cycle_XRjCbX": {
      "type": "hairscripts-hair-cycle",
      "blocks": {
        "cycle_card_CYte8h": {
          "type": "cycle_card",
          "settings": {
            "kicker": "85% of all hairs",
            "title": "Phase 1 — Anagen",
            "description": "<p>Your follicle is on. Actively building your strand. This is where your hair actually grows. Healthy anagen lasts 2–7 years. Every year your follicle stays in this phase is another year of length, density, and thickness accumulating. DHT, elevated cortisol, and nutrient depletion all send the same signal: shut it down early. The timer gets cut short. The strand produced is finer and shorter than the last. Cycle after cycle, that compounds — until the thinning becomes undeniable.</p>"
          }
        },
        "cycle_card_YL4M4M": {
          "type": "cycle_card",
          "settings": {
            "kicker": "3% of all hairs",
            "title": " Phase 2 — Catagen",
            "description": "<p>Your follicle pauses. Prepares to reset. A brief 2–3 week window where the follicle detaches from its blood supply and prepares for the next cycle. This phase is supposed to be short. But a follicle under internal stress — from androgens, inflammation, or poor circulation — enters catagen too early. It didn’t finish the job. It just stopped.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "cycle_card_7KDTxi": {
          "type": "cycle_card",
          "settings": {
            "kicker": "12% of all hairs",
            "title": "Phase 3 — Telogen",
            "description": "<p>Your follicle goes dark. No growth. No strand production. Normally, about 10–15% of your follicles are resting at any time — that’s healthy. But when hormonal disruption, chronic stress, or iron deficiency push more follicles into telogen simultaneously, you lose density fast. And when those follicles finally wake back up, they re-enter anagen producing weaker, thinner strands than before. That’s miniaturization. That’s the real driver behind hormonal hair loss.<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "cycle_card_CYte8h",
        "cycle_card_YL4M4M",
        "cycle_card_7KDTxi"
      ],
